# -- your real, personal config -- never tracked, never overwritten --------
# Generic placeholders ship as the *.example versions (tracked); your real,
# filled-in versions keep their normal filenames on disk and are simply
# invisible to git. Nothing in this project (my-bt, the RPM, build/install
# scripts) ever deletes or overwrites these -- see README.md and
# the maintainer's local notes for the full reasoning.
/settings.toml
/site/index.html
/site/impressum.html
/site/privacy.html
/site/privacy.html.tmpl
/site/terms.html
/site/nginx-locations.conf

# Early drafts of the same real legal content above, kept locally for
# history but not meant for the public template repo.
/legal-notice-suggestion.html
/privacy-policy-suggestion.html
/terms-suggestion.html

# Full design-rationale doc: written for/about this specific deployment
# (real server, real accounts, real legal analysis) -- personal reference,
# not a generic template like README.md.
/SOLUTION-DESIGN.md

# Personal, non-shared dev notes. Deliberately matched by extension
# (*.local.md), not by the literal filename, so this file never has to be
# named in a file that itself gets published.
*.local.md

# -- runtime/local state -----------------------------------------------------
/data/
/secrets/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# -- local build output -------------------------------------------------------
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# -- editor/OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
